                                    </Border>
                                    <Border Style="{StaticResource Group}">
                                        <StackPanel>
                                            <TextBlock Text="Clipboard history" Style="{StaticResource GroupTitle}" />
                                            <CheckBox x:Name="ClipHistoryBox" Click="ClipHistory_Changed">
                                                <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Foreground="{DynamicResource Fg}">Remember the last 50 texts I copy, so chats can use them <Run Foreground="{DynamicResource Dim}" Text="· kept in memory only, gone when Ivo closes; skips what password managers mark as secret, like Windows' own clipboard history does" /></TextBlock>
                                            </CheckBox>
                                        </StackPanel>
                                    </Border>
                                    <Border Style="{StaticResource Group}">
                                        <StackPanel>
                                            <TextBlock Text="How Ivo handles your data" Style="{StaticResource GroupTitle}" />
                                            <TextBlock Foreground="{DynamicResource Fg}" FontSize="12" TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="21"
                                                       Text="•  API keys are encrypted with your Windows account; other users of this PC can&apos;t read them.&#x0a;•  With the app lock on, chats, the Inbox, to-dos, memories, starred replies, projects, the knowledge index, the activity log and API keys are also encrypted with your PIN or password, and backups are sealed with it.&#x0a;•  While Ivo is locked, nothing shows: not the window, the companion, quick capture, screenshots or what notifications are about.&#x0a;•  Messages go only to the provider or agent you pick for a chat. Ivo has no servers and sends no usage data.&#x0a;•  Keys, passwords and card numbers in a message are hidden from cloud models (above). Local-only chats never leave this PC.&#x0a;•  Text from web pages and tools is treated as data, not instructions; after reading it, changes ask you first.&#x0a;•  Every change an agent makes is written to the activity log (above), with secrets masked.&#x0a;•  MCP servers and skills ask before they&apos;re first used, and again if they change. MCP servers can run sandboxed.&#x0a;•  Spending limits and the expensive-model warning ask before a costly request (Settings → Spending).&#x0a;•  Incognito chats are never saved and don&apos;t use or add to memory.&#x0a;•  Scan this PC only reads files and checks local ports; nothing it finds leaves this PC.&#x0a;•  Agents (Claude Code, Copilot…) keep their own sign-ins; Ivo never reads them.&#x0a;•  Spotify lyrics come from LRCLIB (lrclib.net): only the song&apos;s name, artist, album and length are sent, for the lyrics in the Spotify panel, the line being sung in the title bar&apos;s island, and lyrics Ivo&apos;s chat shows when you ask.&#x0a;•  Ivo&apos;s own chat works offline. A word or message she doesn&apos;t know, and songs or artists you ask about, are looked up on free public services (dictionaryapi.dev, Urban Dictionary, DuckDuckGo, Wikipedia): only that word or subject is sent, and what she learns stays on this PC.&#x0a;•  YouTube in Ivo&apos;s chat reads channels&apos; public feeds (youtube.com) with no account; the channels you follow stay on this PC. Reddit uses its official read-only API with an app id you make yourself (no Reddit sign-in); only the subreddit you ask about is sent.&#x0a;•  Webhooks post only the events you pick (a reminder&apos;s words, a task&apos;s result, the briefing, a finished focus session) to the addresses you add; nothing else goes there.&#x0a;•  Text from screen reads the area you pick with Windows&apos; own text recognition, on this PC; the text goes only to your clipboard.&#x0a;•  Notes are kept on this PC (sealed with the app lock like your chats).&#x0a;•  Portal connects two Ivos directly and encrypts everything end to end; no server of Ivo&apos;s is involved. A public address-lookup server (STUN, by Google or Cloudflare) only tells each PC its own internet address, and the joiner&apos;s reply comes back through public message relays (ntfy.sh and the Nostr relays relay.primal.net, nos.lol and relay.damus.io), encrypted with a key that is only in the invite, into a mailbox with a random name. Contacts share only such a mailbox and key, to ring each other. Chats, stickers, pictures and statuses go through the same relays, sealed with the thread&apos;s key (files through ntfy.sh only). While the app runs it tells the Nostr relays once a minute that you&apos;re here, under a scrambled name only your contacts can work out, so they see you online and when you were last seen; Invisible sends nothing; groups hand their key to each member sealed for them alone. Ask Ivo in a Portal uses your own model; nothing of your keys or chats is shared, only the lines you send." />
                                        </StackPanel>
                                    </Border>
                                </StackPanel>

